This is CCZE, a fast log colorizer written in C, intended to be a
drop-in replacement for colorize (http://colorize.raszi.hu).

macOS build (Apple Silicon or Intel)
-----------------------------------

Install the Xcode Command Line Tools if `cc --version` is unavailable
(`xcode-select --install`), then install the regex dependency with Homebrew:

    brew install pcre2

From the source directory, build and install without sudo:

    ./configure --prefix="$HOME/.local" --with-builtins=all
    make
    make check
    make install

`make install` creates $HOME/.local and the required subdirectories if
needed. You do not need to create them manually.

Ensure $HOME/.local/bin is on your PATH.

For fish, run once:

    fish_add_path "$HOME/.local/bin"

For Bash, add this line to ~/.bash_profile for login shells, or ~/.bashrc
for non-login interactive shells:

    export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"

For Zsh, add this line to ~/.zshrc:

    export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"

After editing the Bash or Zsh configuration, open a new terminal.

Colorize a log stream with ANSI output (also suitable for pipes):

    tail -f /path/to/service.log | ccze -A -o nolookups

Use `ccze --help` for options and `ccze -l` for supported log formats.
Omit `-A` for the original curses display, or use `-h` for HTML output.
The build above includes all bundled plugins in the executable, so no
separate plugin installation is needed.

CCZE uses PCRE2's 8-bit library, not the legacy PCRE library. Existing
third-party plugins must be ported to ccze-regex.h and rebuilt (plugin ABI 3).
The PCRE_CONFIG configure variable, if set, must point to pcre2-config.

See the NEWS file for a description of recent changes to CCZE.

See the file INSTALL for instructions on how to build and install the
CCZE data and program files. See the CCZE manual for details about
configuration. Type "man ccze" in the shell prompt.

Please visit the official CCZE web page for more information. The URL
is http://bonehunter.rulez.org/CCZE.html.
